<!--
    kuna `returndup auto`, the default: in an optimized function, a shared
    return of a value the arms merge (`if (c) v = f(); else { ...; v = -1; }
    return v;`) gives each arm its own return, as the source wrote it.

    Stage / sub-stage: P8 "goto-quality", before the final structuring:
    `returndup` splits the return block (kuna_retshape::arm_returns finds it)
    after the join the stripped stack-protector check left is spliced into it.
    The P0 assertion `option returndup record` keeps the merged return.

    The image is decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/
    retshape_gcc_O2_x86_64, loaded whole.  `describe` returns -1 after an
    error message or the result of `measure`; the canary check joins both
    paths before one exit.  `wrap_add` updates the value it returns in one arm
    (`if (res < data) res += knob;`) and keeps its one return.

    Pass 1 runs with the default: describe returns in each arm, wrap_add keeps
    its update.  Pass 2 (`option returndup record`) prints describe's merged
    variable.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">c3</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/retshape_gcc_O2_x86_64</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load function describe</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load function wrap_add</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option returndup record</com>
  <com>load function describe</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
</script>
